  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Before the wolf tide, Fang Yuan judges that hunting alone requires a scouting or movement-type Gu, otherwise he will fall to the pack.",
      "chapters": [
        122
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Without a movement Gu worm he cannot catch Bai Ning Bing in a chase.",
      "chapters": [
        138
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_ning_bing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rainbow light Gu is a rank three movement Gu that turns the user into light to escape. Narration calls it the fastest among rank three movement Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        266
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "mortal-speed-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_rainbow_light_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At auction, chasing wind Gu is sold as a rank four movement Gu that lets a Gu Master chase after winds. Wind, light, lightning, and cloud are named outstanding types among movement Gu worms.",
      "chapters": [
        307
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "outstanding-mortal-types",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_chasing_wind_gu",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dream Travel, Carefree Travel, Fixed Immortal Travel, and Liquor God Travel are listed as the four great movement Gu. Dream Travel lets Gu Masters enter other people’s dreams. Carefree Travel is best at dodging attacks. Fixed Immortal Travel teleports the user to a chosen place. Liquor God Travel is called the most special and first appears in The Legends of Ren Zu.",
      "chapters": [
        307
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "four-great-movement-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_dream_travel",
        "gu_carefree_travel",
        "gu_fixed_immortal_travel",
        "gu_liquor_god_travel",
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Divine Travel Gu is a rank six Immortal Gu whose earliest appearance is in The Legends of Ren Zu, beside Verdant Great Sun after liquor aura congealed into the Gu. It can send the Gu Master anywhere, but activation requires a drunken state and the destination cannot be controlled. Narration places Divine Travel among the four great movement Gu, then notes Verdant Great Sun refined it into Fixed Immortal Travel Gu, which is also among those four and needs a concrete impression of the destination.",
      "chapters": [
        378
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "divine-travel-among-the-four",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_divine_travel",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "char_verdant_great_sun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu as living tools are covered on Gu worms. Attack among the six classifications is covered on Attack Gu.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
